{
  "id": "unit-plan",
  "kind": "unit-plan",
  "description": "planUnitSync. 1: no remote file: local stored as is, document written. 2: equal: nothing. 3: remote newer record: stored locally, no write. 4: local newer: write only. 5: a collection only on the remote is stored (also an unknown one). 6: a collection only on the local side is kept and written. 7: both sides have a record the other lacks. 8: an empty collection missing remotely is written, no local change. 9: remote has a newer unit name. 10: local has the newer unit name. 11: other unit id. 12: other kind. 13: moved: merged state, moved reported, no write. 14: rejected entries carry the collection name, by key and by index. 15: a record with a bad time on the remote is dropped and the remote rewritten. 16: collections merge independently. 17: a place kind works the same.",
  "source": "docs/sync.md",
